VeridianOS: the time data engine's own translation domain only

The top-level CMakeLists.txt defines TRANSLATION_DOMAIN as
"libplasma5support" for the whole tree; each data engine directory
removes that definition before adding its own, except the time engine's,
so its sources were compiled with both (GCC: "'TRANSLATION_DOMAIN'
redefined") and took whichever came last on the command line. It now
removes it like the others.

--- a/src/dataengines/time/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/dataengines/time/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+remove_definitions(-DTRANSLATION_DOMAIN=\"libplasma5support\")
 add_definitions(-DTRANSLATION_DOMAIN=\"plasma_engine_time\")
 
 set(time_engine_SRCS
